Greetings, adventurers! We hope you've been enjoying [i]Questlist[/i].

If you don't have the game yet, now it's a great time to purchase it! It will be 20% off for the two weeks of the Steam Summer Sales.

Today's small patch introduces the following bugfixes:
[list][*]Fixed a bug that would make the game crash against the Sandworm in the Southills. The bug triggered when the boss [spoiler]would hid underground, becoming impossible to target[/spoiler], all the adds were killed, and Sunny used an offensive brew. She won't be able to use offensive concoctions anymore;
[*]Fixed a bug with the 'three boulders, three switches' puzzle in the Emerald Maze 3;
[*]Fixed an animation to properly centering on the slime in the sewers;
[/list]

Thank you for playing!

Greetings! We hope you have been enjoying [i]Questlist[/i]. Today's patch includes the following:
[h3]Changes to NG+[/h3]
[i]Questlist[/i] was designed with replayability in mind. Routes are complete experiences from start to finish, but focus on one specific perspective or theme; some only include happy endings, other routes only include tragic endings, some have a mix. 
Playing multiple routes enriches the story by showing the full picture.

To make replaying the game more enjoyable, we introduced NG+ some weeks ago.
Today we want to make some changes to it that will make it even easier to replay the game:
[list][*]Level, skill and equipment inheritance[/list]You will be able to inherit Vera's level, Vera's skill levels (so you'll start with [i]Dangerous Lips++[/i], for example), gold and equipment. You'll inherit one of all the jewels you already own: if you have two of the same jewels (for example, two [i]Water Strikes[/i]), you'll only inherit one. The levels of party members will match Vera's.

[b]IMPORTANT![/b] Level and equipment inheritance is [b]not retroactive[/b]: you'll need to watch the ending credits at least once to unlock it. We hope this change will make it easier for players to focus on the multiple paths of the story.
[h3]Balance changes[/h3]
[list][*]Enemies have been made scarcer in some areas. Less enemies are required to complete certain quests. The EXP & items they reward has been increased;[/list][i]Developer's notes[/i]: the areas most affected were Ostmoor, the Southills, the highways and most caves; this should remove the feel of grinding.
[list][*]Lowered HP & damage of the first Raina fight on Easy and Normal difficulties;
[*]Further decrease of damage and Freeze chance of the last boss on all difficulties;
[*]The slot machines in the casino have been reworked to be much more generous;[/list][i]Developer's notes[/i]: Dice Delight is the best way to make tokens, but players seem to enjoy the slots a lot. We decided to adjust the winning chances to make the spins feel more rewarding.
[h3]Miscellaneous fixes[/h3]
[list][*]Added a pop-up after unlocking the monkey's boon;
[*]Fixed a bug that made party members leave with accessories;
[*]Sunny's unique accessories will now be removed once she leaves the party;
[*]Fixed a bug that caused a softlock if the second floor of Lovett's tower was accessed from the left hallway;
[*]Minor text fixes;[/list]
Thank you for playing!

Greetings! We hope you've been enjoying [i]Questlist[/i].
We just released a hotfix to the live & BETA build of the game. Here's what changed:
[h1]Live branch[/h1]
[h2]Balance changes[/h2]
[list]
[*]Health potions now restore 50 more HP, and should feel more effective in the early game. [/list]
[h2]Bug fixes[/h2]
[list]
[*]The option to disable mouse input is now available from the main menu, and is OFF by default. This does not affect current savefiles;
[*]Fixed a softlock caused by the rafts in the sewers;
[*]Fixed Reniel automatically switching to Avenger stance against a normal difficulty imp;
[*]Fixed a softlock caused by a boulder in the third stretch of the Emerald Maze;
[*]Fixed an issue that allowed you to complete the 'Rumors of assembly' quest before unlocking it;
[*]Clarified what players need to do to complete the 'Not my kind of spelunking' quest;
[*]You can now access the VIP area of the Stout if you have the pass, regardless of story progression. You'll still need to talk with the clerk at the Guild Affairs Office to progress;
[*]Removed a dev-only shortcut to skip the cave underneath the spa;
[*]Fixed a softlock caused by Dana vibing outside of her house on Celia's day 19;
[*]Fixed CG 18 unlocking in Celia's route but not Lyra's;
[*]Fixed CG 11 not unlocking properly;[/list]
[h2]More changes[/h2]
We removed the forced conversion to .webp of our images. This will hopefully improve performance, but it makes for a [i]big [/i]download.
We also fixed a bunch of typos. Seeing those float around always makes us sad.
[h2]Troubleshooting[/h2]
A small amount of users have reported freezing. If you're one of them, you can do the following:
[list]
[*]Update your drivers
[*]Disable V-Sync
[*]You can try switching to the BETA branch
[/list]
[h1]What is the BETA branch?[/h1]
The BETA branch uses an older version of the framework that is compatible with Windows 7.
If you're experiencing freezes, it might be worth switching to the BETA branch!
It just received an update with all the above fixes, plus a further downgrade of the framework that should fix the disappearing textboxes / battler flickering.

